  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Jeuveau maintained its U.S. market share with unit growth and stable pricing, while account penetration expanded further and reorder rates remained healthy. The Evolus Rewards loyalty program continued to grow, deepening consumer stickiness, and international sales provided additional geographic reach. Underlying demand proved resilient in a seasonally weak first quarter, even against a strong prior-year period, signaling steady momentum in the aesthetic neurotoxin market.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** The company delivered a second consecutive quarter of positive adjusted EBITDA, a direct result of last year’s cost-structure overhaul. Leadership reaffirmed full-year guidance for solid revenue growth and full-year profitability, demonstrating conviction in the improved operating model. Achieving profitability during the softest seasonal quarter bolsters management’s credibility around the turnaround narrative and disciplined expense control, positioning the business as increasingly self-sustaining.",
